#: src/features/pnrr/components/PnrrAnomalyInfoPanel.tsx:113
msgid "The filters are calculated automatically from reported data. They help with prioritization; they do not prove an irregularity on their own."
msgstr "The filters are calculated automatically from reported data. They help with prioritization; they do not prove an irregularity on their own."

#: src/features/pnrr/components/filters/PnrrInfoSheet.tsx:99
msgid "The geographic location of the project. National projects without a specific location are marked separately and can be included or excluded from filters."
msgstr "The geographic location of the project. National projects without a specific location are marked separately and can be included or excluded from filters."

#: src/features/pnrr/components/filters/PnrrInfoSheet.tsx:83
msgid "The measure code combines the component code and measure code (for example: C4.I1, C15.I9). It is unique within the component."
msgstr "The measure code combines the component code and measure code (for example: C4.I1, C15.I9). It is unique within the component."

#: src/features/pnrr/components/filters/PnrrInfoSheet.tsx:247
msgid "The original data is expressed in EUR. Displayed values are automatically converted to the currency selected in account settings using fixed reference rates."
msgstr "The original data is expressed in EUR. Displayed values are automatically converted to the currency selected in account settings using fixed reference rates."

#: src/features/pnrr/components/tabs/PnrrOverview.tsx:215
msgid "The percentage represents the share of project value in the component out of the total PNRR value. The background bar visualizes this share. Click a row to filter projects."
msgstr "The percentage represents the share of project value in the component out of the total PNRR value. The background bar visualizes this share. Click a row to filter projects."

#: src/features/pnrr/components/tabs/PnrrOverview.tsx:227
msgid "The percentage represents the share of project value in the county out of the total PNRR value. The background bar visualizes this share. Click a row to filter projects."
msgstr "The percentage represents the share of project value in the county out of the total PNRR value. The background bar visualizes this share. Click a row to filter projects."

#: src/features/pnrr/lib/anomaly-definitions.ts:113
msgid "The same project has different values or progress"
msgstr "The same project has different values or progress"

#: src/features/pnrr/components/filters/PnrrInfoSheet.tsx:223
msgid "The same project is reported with different values, progress, or location."
msgstr "The same project is reported with different values, progress, or location."

#: src/features/pnrr/components/filters/PnrrInfoSheet.tsx:122
msgid "The top-level sector filter is exhaustive: every project is classified as either public or private / non-public, so the two values add up to the total under the same active filters."
msgstr "The top-level sector filter is exhaustive: every project is classified as either public or private / non-public, so the two values add up to the total under the same active filters."

#: src/features/pnrr/components/filters/PnrrInfoSheet.tsx:45
msgid "This dashboard shows all projects in Romania's National Recovery and Resilience Plan (PNRR). The data is sourced from the Ministry of Investments and European Projects."
msgstr "This dashboard shows all projects in Romania's National Recovery and Resilience Plan (PNRR). The data is sourced from the Ministry of Investments and European Projects."

#: src/features/pnrr/lib/anomaly-definitions.ts:114
msgid "This filter marks projects that appear multiple times with the same core identity but different information. This is a data interpretation issue: it may be an incomplete update, subcomponent reporting, or an import error."
msgstr "This filter marks projects that appear multiple times with the same core identity but different information. This is a data interpretation issue: it may be an incomplete update, subcomponent reporting, or an import error."

#: src/features/pnrr/lib/anomaly-definitions.ts:124
msgid "This filter shows large projects with missing financial progress. Missing data does not automatically mean no payments were made; it may mean financial data was not published or was not updated in this snapshot."
msgstr "This filter shows large projects with missing financial progress. Missing data does not automatically mean no payments were made; it may mean financial data was not published or was not updated in this snapshot."

#: src/features/pnrr/lib/anomaly-definitions.ts:101
msgid "This filter shows projects reported as technically completed but with financial progress below 80%. This is not automatically an irregularity: payments may follow acceptance. Still, a large gap can indicate blocked acceptance, incomplete documents, or disputes."
msgstr "This filter shows projects reported as technically completed but with financial progress below 80%. This is not automatically an irregularity: payments may follow acceptance. Still, a large gap can indicate blocked acceptance, incomplete documents, or disputes."

#: src/features/pnrr/lib/anomaly-definitions.ts:81
msgid "This filter shows projects where financial progress is far above technical progress. It may be a legitimate advance payment or a delay in technical reporting, but it matters because the money appears to have moved faster than delivery."
msgstr "This filter shows projects where financial progress is far above technical progress. It may be a legitimate advance payment or a delay in technical reporting, but it matters because the money appears to have moved faster than delivery."

#: src/features/pnrr/lib/anomaly-definitions.ts:71
msgid "This filter shows projects where reported financial progress exceeds 100%. In a clean dataset, a project should not exceed its reported value without an explanation: budget change, delayed correction, or reporting error."
msgstr "This filter shows projects where reported financial progress exceeds 100%. In a clean dataset, a project should not exceed its reported value without an explanation: budget change, delayed correction, or reporting error."

#: src/features/pnrr/lib/anomaly-definitions.ts:134
msgid "This filter shows technically completed projects worth more than one million euros but with no published financial progress. It matters for analysis quality because delivery cannot be compared with reimbursement."
msgstr "This filter shows technically completed projects worth more than one million euros but with no published financial progress. It matters for analysis quality because delivery cannot be compared with reimbursement."

#: src/features/pnrr/lib/anomaly-definitions.ts:91
msgid "This filter surfaces large projects that still have low technical progress. The EUR 10 million threshold keeps the list focused on projects with high budget impact. The “in implementation” status is interpreted as under 30% only for this filter."
msgstr "This filter surfaces large projects that still have low technical progress. The EUR 10 million threshold keeps the list focused on projects with high budget impact. The “in implementation” status is interpreted as under 30% only for this filter."

